.TH NOTM-TEST-HARNESS 7 "2026-06-26" "notm 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
notm-test-harness \- developer test harness for notm
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B notm
developer test harness is a local UI-driving test harness used for fixture
testing, smoke
tests, and agent-assisted validation.  It is not mail automation, filtering, or
rules support.  It is disabled by default.  Normal desktop users should launch
.B notm launch
without the test harness.
.PP
Each request is one JSON line containing a
.B token,
.B command,
and optional
.B args
object.  Commands run in the GTK main loop and operate on the real application
state.
.SH NORMAL OPERATION
Normal desktop mail use does not require this harness.
Start notm normally with:
.PP
.nf
notm launch
.fi
.PP
Use the harness only when developing, debugging, or running smoke tests.
.SH TEST-HARNESS LAUNCH
.nf
notm launch \\
  --test-harness \\
  --test-harness-socket /tmp/notm.sock \\
  --test-harness-token dev-token
.fi
.PP
Fixture mode is preferred for UI test-harness runs that do not require a live
mailbox:
.PP
.nf
notm launch --fixture \\
  --test-harness \\
  --test-harness-socket /tmp/notm.sock \\
  --test-harness-token dev-token
.fi
.SH TEST REQUEST EXAMPLE
.nf
{"token":"dev-token","command":"run_search","args":{"query":"tag:inbox"}}
.fi
