.SH SAFETY
Keep the socket local to the user session and use a token.  Prefer fixture data
for test-harness runs.  Fixture mode does not run configured receive,
database-update, or external-send commands; sends are captured locally and tag
changes are confined to the disposable fixture database.
.PP
On a non-fixture account,
.B automation.allow_live_send_test
must be true for
.B compose_send
and
.B automation.allow_live_tag_test
must be true for tag mutations.  Both default to false, and the gates also
apply when the operation is requested through
.BR run_command .
Non-fixture sync retains its separate explicit
.B [sync]
enablement.  Draft and attachment commands can change configured local files
and are intentionally outside the send/tag gates; invoke them only when those
file changes are intended.
